Error [E0149]: a runtime `String` can't be used as `HTML`
  --> tests/ui/typed_text_string_into_html.jet:6:12
    |
  6 |     render(user_input)
    |            ^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: interpolating untrusted text into a query or page is how injection happens; only a checked literal (its `{value}` holes become bound parameters or escaped insertions) may build one
 Fix: write `HTML.{"..."}` with `{value}` holes, or use `HTML.raw("…")` if you have audited the text
